  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Finely chop garlic.\n• In a medium saucepan, melt the butter with a dash of olive oil over medium heat. Cook half the garlic until fragrant, 1-2 minutes. Add basmati rice, the water (for the rice) and a generous pinch of salt. Stir, then bring to the boil. Reduce heat to low and cover with a lid.\n• Cook for 10 minutes, then remove from heat. Keep covered, until rice is tender and water is absorbed, 10 minutes. TIP: The rice will finish cooking in its own steam, so don't peek!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-64d066596ea5936499250af5-11c4b714.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, thinly slice brown onion.\n• Thinly slice capsicum.\n• Trim and halve green beans.\n• Thinly slice long chilli (if using).\n• Drain and rinse lentils.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-64d066596ea5936499250af5-93557607.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over high heat. Cook onion and capsicum, stirring, until softened, 3-4 minutes. Add green beans and lentils and cook until almost tender, 3-4 minutes.\n• Reduce heat to medium-high. Add Bengal curry paste, Mumbai spice blend and remaining garlic and cook until fragrant, 1-2 minutes.\n• Add the brown sugar, coconut milk (see ingredients) and the water (for the curry). Simmer, stirring, until thickened slightly, 2-4 minutes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-64d066596ea5936499250af5-b53db495.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide garlic rice between bowls. Top with Bengal lentil and veggie curry.\n• Tear over coriander leaves.\n• Sprinkle with chilli to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-64d066596ea5936499250af5-352946a1.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
